{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]Must be getting [F#]early, [B][E]clocks are running [A][E]late,
[F#]Paint-by-number morning sky, looks so [B][E]phony.
[B]Dawn is breaking [F#][B]everywhere, [E]light a candle,curse [A]the [E]glare,
[F#]Draw the curtains, I don't [B]care, 'cause [E]it's alright.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#]I  [B]will get [E]by,
[F#]I  [B]will get [E]by,
[F#]I  [B]will get [A][E]by,[F#]
I will [E]survive.[A][E][B][F#][B][F#]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I see you've got your fist out, say your piece and get out,
Yes I get the gist of it, but it's all right.
Sorry that you feel that way, the only thing I meant to say,
Every silver lining's got a touch of grey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C#m]It's a [C#7]lesson to [F#]me,[B][F#]
the [C#m]Ables and the [C#7]Bakers and the [F#]C's[B][F#]
[G#m]The [D#]ABC's    [C#m7]we all must [F#]face, [B7]and try to [E7]keep a little [F#]grace
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
It's a lesson to me, the deltas and the east and the freeze
The ABCs, we all think of, and try to give a little love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I know the rent is in arrears, the dog has not been fed in years,
It's even worse than it appears, but it's all right.
The cow is giving kerosene, kid can't read at seventeen,
The words he knows are all obscene, but it's all right.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
The shoe is on the hand it fits, there's really nothing much to it
Whistle through your teeth and spit, 'cause, it's all right.
Oh, well, a Touch of Grey, kind of suits you anyway
That was all I had to say, it's all right.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I will get by, I will get by
I will get by, I will survive
We will get by, we will get by
We will get by, we will survive
{end_of_verse}
